    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/releases/tag/b11730"/>
    <title>b11730: cuda: cap MMQ Stream-K blocks at available work (#30553)</title>
    <content type="html">&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;cuda: cap Stream-K blocks at the number of k-blocks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stream-K normally launches one CUDA block per SM. For small matrices,&lt;br&gt;
this can exceed the total number of output-tile/k-block pairs, leaving&lt;br&gt;
blocks with no work and adding launch and fixup overhead. Cap the grid&lt;br&gt;
at that count to remove these excess blocks without changing the useful&lt;br&gt;
rounded K ranges or numerical results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Assisted-by: Codex&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;cuda: cap Stream-K blocks at the number of k iterations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cap the grid at the number of K_vram iterations across all output tiles, rounding up partial iterations. This removes extra CUDA blocks left by the k-block cap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partial iterations can change FP32 summation grouping. MUL_MAT and MUL_MAT_ID backend tests pass on RTX 5090.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Update ggml/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Co-authored-by: Johannes Gäßler &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:johannesg@5d6.de&quot;&gt;johannesg@5d6.de&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</content>
