    <content type="html">&lt;details open=&quot;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;tools : reject truncated GGUF tensor data in split and export tools (&lt;a class=&quot;issue-link js-issue-link&quot; data-error-text=&quot;Failed to load title&quot; data-id=&quot;5843477558&quot; data-permission-text=&quot;Title is private&quot; data-url=&quot;https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/30497&quot; data-hovercard-type=&quot;pull_request&quot; data-hovercard-url=&quot;/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/30497/hovercard&quot; href=&quot;https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/30497&quot;&gt;#30497&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The problem here in the repo is gguf-split can silently produce corrupted tensor output when the input GGUF file is truncated. The fix is to add tensor-data bounds checks and short-read checks in gguf-split.cpp and export-lora.cpp, and a regression test that checks truncated input is rejected and valid tensor data is preserved.#&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bug : GGUF-split can silently produce corrupted tensor output when the input GGUF file is truncated. Fix : add short-read checks in gguf-split.cpp (in copy_file_to_file in split_strategy) and export-lora.cpp (in read_tensor_data of file_input) so that truncated input is rejected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;
